{"text": "Teens Out-Yell Beatles\nWILL LEONARD\n\nChicago Tribune (1963-Current file); Aug 21, 1965;\nProQuest Historical Newspapers Chicago Tribune (1849 - 1987)\n\npg. 1\n\nTeens Out-Yell Beatles\n\nBut, Britons Like\nBeing Center\nof Uproar\n\nBY WILL LEONARD\n(Pictures on back page)\nMore than 50,000 teen-agers,\n90 per cent of them girls,\nscreamed the Beatles into ob-\nlivion yesterday in two per-\nformances in White Sox park.\nScarcely a note was heard.\njump-\ning with joy. Some fainted but\nthere were no injuries. Even\nthe Beatles liked it.\n\u201cThey pay good prices to get\nin, Who are we to say whether\nor not they should scream?\u201d\nsaid Beatle John Lennon, 24,\nwhen asked at a between-shows\npress conference whether it\nbothered him to be shouted\ndown.\n\n200 Interview Them\n\nMore than 200 persons, some\nof them reporters, jammed the\nWhite Sox\u2019s Bards\u2019 room for\nthe press conference, and al-\nmost everybody agreed that the\nmop-haired Liverpudlians were\npretty cute in their replies.\nP. W. R, C. Haley, deputy\n\nDiane Olsen, 13, of 6052 S.\nMulligan av., sobbing because\nshe couldn\u2019t get near Beatles\nat airport. {TRIBUNE Statf Photo}\n\nBritish consul general in Chi-\ncago, spoke up from the back\n\u2018of the room:\n\u201cDo you think you're doing a\ngood job for your country?\u201d\n\u201cYes, do you?\u201d shot back\nLennon.\nHaley laughed and told the\nfour subjects of the queen \u2014\nthey recently won the Order of\nthe British Empire, to the\namazement of many and the\n\nconsternation of some\u2014that he\nthought they were doing a good\njob.\nTo some of the questions\nabout their likes, dislikes, loves,\nand habits, the Beatles had a\nstock answer:\n\u201cLawt 0\u00b0 rubbish.\u201d\nAsked About Songs\nA girl reporter asked what\nthey thought of a comment that\n\u201cyou could be great song writ-\ners if you wanted to.\u201d\n\u201cWell,\u201d said Beatle Paul Mc-\nCartney, 23, \u201cwe write what\nwe feel like at the moment like\nCole Porter did. People will like\nus a lot more when we're older,\nyou just watch.\u201d\nApparently, rowdyism Thurs-\nday night cut short the Beatles\u2019\nPerformance in Houston, and\nthey were asked about it.\nHad Trouble in Houston\n\u201cThey sent about 25 cops out\nto take care of 5,000 kids,\u201d Mc-\nCartney replied. \u201cIn every town\nthey think, \u2018Our kids are dif-\nferent; they have common\nsense.\u2019 That just shows you the\nway some policemen think.\u201d\nBehavior at Houston was\namong the worst they encoun-\n\n[Continued on page 2, col. 6]\n\nReproduced with permission of the copyright owner. Further reproduction prohibited without permission.",
